# Rust Backend UI Convention

When exposing a Rust backend capability through a desktop UI, use the Tauri/React Hub frontend and its shared visual system.

- Prefer the existing Tauri/React shell under `src/kyth-hub-web/src/`.
- Reuse its shared tokens and components, especially `src/styles/theme.css`, cards, navigation, buttons, status pills, and responsive grids.
- Keep Rust responsible for commands, privileged operations, system state, and data; keep layout, presentation, and interaction composition in React.
- Do not introduce a separate visual language or default to a new native UI toolkit for a Rust-backed feature.
- Preserve viewport-safe responsive behavior: content must remain contained and usable at the supported window sizes.
- The Hub has no Slint shell — Tauri/React is the only Hub UI, and `tests/test_kyth_hub_native_contract.py` guards against a Slint binary or `ui/hub.slint` reappearing. Do not add one back without the user explicitly requesting it.
